### ===== PART 1: acks (stop/start brokers between these - see README) =====

### 1. acks=all
POST http://localhost:8080/api/acks/all?message=hello-all

### 2. acks=1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/acks/1?message=hello-one

### 3. acks=0 (offset will be -1)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/acks/0?message=hello-zero


### ===== PART 2: hot partitions =====

### 4. Clear the stats
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/page-views/stats

### 5. 500 page views, 80% from big-merchant -> one hot partition
POST http://localhost:8080/api/page-views?count=500&salted=false

### 6. Processed so far, per partition (run it a few times)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/page-views/stats

### 7. Same traffic, but with key salting
POST http://localhost:8080/api/page-views?count=500&salted=true


### ===== PART 3: dual write vs outbox =====

### 8. Dual write + crash -> Kafka event sent, DB rolled back = GHOST event
POST http://localhost:8080/api/payments/dual-write?fail=true
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId":"cust-1","amount":5000}

### 9. Payments in the DB (the ghost payment is NOT here)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/payments

### 10. Outbox + crash -> nothing saved, nothing sent
POST http://localhost:8080/api/payments?fail=true
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId":"cust-1","amount":5000}

### 11. Outbox happy path -> relay publishes within 2 seconds
POST http://localhost:8080/api/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId":"cust-2","amount":12500}

### 12. Outbox table (look at publishedAt)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/outbox

### 13. Send the same event again -> consumer skips the DUPLICATE
### Copy an "id" from request #12 into the URL
POST http://localhost:8080/api/outbox/PASTE-EVENT-ID-HERE/republish
